==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]].
*1 [[The Face]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 5~6.67 seconds<sup>150f~200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*15 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*5 [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A fairly cookie-cutter stage that uses burrowing Zombies to pierce your defenses while having the Surge Base clean up your frontline attackers. You'll have to preserve ground using the [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] and whatever anti-Zombies you have at your disposal, before then chipping down The Face once the smoke clears. [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] is preferable to [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], as he's more cost-efficient and outranges Zir Zeal, but both suffice.

[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] is the meatshield of choice here, accompanied by Research [[Cat Combo]]s of course. [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] should generally be good enough to deal with The Face. [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] or [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]] (If you have it), can help thin out the Zombies together with Cat Chief/Cadaver BearCat. If you are still lacking in DPS, then bring [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] to help with cleanup.

