==Trivia==
*Cookie Cutter Ruins's Japanese name, Katanuki Iseki (かたぬき移籍, "Katanuki Ruins") is a reference to the candy-carving festival activity ''[[wikipedia:Katanuki|Katanuki]]''.
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], the stage width was set to 5,400. The change was made because of a bug in how [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|Animated Bases]] spawn when not set as bosses.

